 ## Retries
 
-A capture that times out is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all, one after the other.
+A capture that times out is tried again according to the [attempt limit and growing pauses in the capture
+implementation](../../larder/capture.py). If every attempt times out, the timeout is raised to the caller.
+
+During the gateway's Friday peak, immediate retries all landed in the same slow period: 58 confirmed pantry orders
+went uncharged and a volunteer captured them by hand the next morning. A sandbox replay with spaced retries would
+have recovered 57 of those orders. The team accepted up to 20 seconds of added waiting on the confirmation page to
+reduce that manual work. Switching gateways was deferred because the contract runs to December 2026. These findings
+and the accepted trade-off came from [issue 40](../../notes/issue-40.md).
 
